# headwear/helm/leathercap: the Leather cap (P2c slice, SLICE-HELM-SHIELD; band1, the archer's): a close boiled-leather
# arming cap, matte and warm (no glint: a lit left plane in leather 3, the turn in 2, the shadowed right in 1), a stitched
# seam over the crown and a rolled band lit along its top, its lower edge on the brow row (F-25 man, F-24 woman) so the eyes
# show under it. Volume styles draw their capped views (the `capped` flag); '-' masks the hair above the band. Shared by
# both bodies (D10). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-HEAD iteration 3) the crown in leather, the band dyed in the arms colour (cloth1), short ear flaps: a
# leather arming cap, never a knitted beanie.
# Regions (P2c ladder slice, LADDER-HEAD; contracts 3b) mark the rim band R, its socket G and the brow band P; pixels unchanged.
use person
body adult
role helm band1
layer headwear
anchor head
keys rest
tags overlay

